# NVLink / NVSwitch intra-server domain for the 1024-GPU rail cluster.
#
#   128 servers x 8 GPUs. Tier 0 leaf = ONE server's NVSwitch: 8 GPUs on a single
#   3600 Gbps (450 GB/s per direction, NVLink4-class) non-blocking crossbar.
#   Classic CONSECUTIVE attachment (NO "Rails" line): leaf s owns GPUs 8s..8s+7,
#   which is exactly one server -- so intra-server traffic stays on the leaf.
#
#   Only intra-server flows are ever attached to this topology (see the
#   connect-time selection in main_roce/main_uec), so traffic NEVER leaves a
#   leaf. Tier 1 exists solely because htsim requires >= 2 tiers; it is inert.
#   That also sidesteps the fabric-inflation problem: the upper tier is never
#   used, so its (over-provisioned) sizing is irrelevant.
Nodes 1024
Tiers 2
Podsize 1024

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 8
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 8
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 100
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 128
Downlink_Latency_ns 100
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1
